  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Study Black Soldier Fly for local animal feed production</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Palestinian Territories have been very dependent on imports for many of their food commodities and observe increasing structural vulnerability being this dependent. In addition, Palestinians face shrinking access to grasing lands due to settler violence and establishment of new settlements. There is a need to become more self-sufficient in food production. Building (partial) animal-feed resilience through local production is vital. Black Soldier Fly farming has emerged globally as a promising solution to convert organic waste streams into valuable products, such as insect larvae as a source of protein for animal feed, insect oil and organic fertiliser. It can contribute to local feed production, waste reduction, circular and regenerative agriculture, also in Palestinian Territories. Before moving into this direction however, several critical conditions and a healthy business case in this context are to be clarified, which is what this study entails.</narrative>
  </description>
